<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>General theory for two-parameter weak approximation.</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in(0,\min\{1,T\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in(0,\min\{1,T\})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>. We consider the general discrete iteration</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{k+1}\;=\;x_{k}+\eta\,h\bigl(x_{k},\gamma_{k},\eta,\rho\bigr),\qquad x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\quad k=0,1,\dots,N," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k+1}\;=\;x_{k}+\eta\,h\bigl(x_{k},\gamma_{k},\eta,\rho\bigr),\qquad x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\quad k=0,1,\dots,N,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and its corresponding continuous-time approximation by the SDE</p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}X_{t}\;=\;b\bigl(X_{t},\eta,\rho\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}t\;+\;\sqrt{\eta}\,\sigma\bigl(X_{t},\eta,\rho\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}W_{t},\qquad X_{0}=x_{0},\;t\in[0,T]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}X_{t}\;=\;b\bigl(X_{t},\eta,\rho\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}t\;+\;\sqrt{\eta}\,\sigma\bigl(X_{t},\eta,\rho\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}W_{t},\qquad X_{0}=x_{0},\;t\in[0,T].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We denote <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{X}_{k}:=X_{k\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{X}_{k}:=X_{k\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the one-step changes:</p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(x):=x_{1}-x,\qquad\widetilde{\Delta}(x):=\widetilde{X}_{1}-x." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(x):=x_{1}-x,\qquad\widetilde{\Delta}(x):=\widetilde{X}_{1}-x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Following the SDE framework by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mil’shtein, (1986)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., (2017)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Compagnoni et al., (2023)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo et al., (2025)</a></cite>, we have the following definition:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of continuous functions <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> of at most polynomial growth, i.e. <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G</annotation></semantics></math> if there exists positive integers <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{1},\kappa_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{1},\kappa_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|g(x)|\leq\kappa_{1}(1+\|x\|^{2\kappa_{2}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|g(x)|\leq\kappa_{1}(1+\|x\|^{2\kappa_{2}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, for each integer <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> we denote by <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> the set of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-times continuously differentiable functions <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> which, together with its partial derivatives up to and
including order <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, belong to <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This definition comes from the field of numerical analysis of SDEs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mil’shtein,, 1986</a>)</cite>. In the case of <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)=||x||^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)=||x||^{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, the bound restricts the difference between the <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th moments of the discrete process and those of the continuous process. We write <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\eta^{\alpha}\rho^{\beta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\eta^{\alpha}\rho^{\beta})</annotation></semantics></math> to denote that there exists a function <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in G</annotation></semantics></math> independent of <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho,\ \eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho,\ \eta</annotation></semantics></math>, such that the error terms are bounded by <math id="A1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\eta^{\alpha}\rho^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\eta^{\alpha}\rho^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Adaption of Theorem 3 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., (2019)</a></cite>)
Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in(0,\min\{1,T\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in(0,\min\{1,T\})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> be an integer. Suppose further that the following conditions hold:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{1}\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{1}\in G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, independent of </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta,\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta,\rho</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, such that for each </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1,2,\dots,\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1,2,\dots,\alpha</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and any indices </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{1},\dots,i_{s}\in\{1,\dots,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{1},\dots,i_{s}\in\{1,\dots,d\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\biggl|\mathbb{E}\!\prod_{j=1}^{s}\Delta_{(i_{j})}(x)\;-\;\mathbb{E}\!\prod_{j=1}^{s}\widetilde{\Delta}_{(i_{j})}(x)\biggr|\;\leq\;K_{1}(x)\,(\eta^{\alpha+1}+\eta\rho^{\beta+1})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.664em;" width="0.664em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.664em;" width="0.664em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\biggl|\mathbb{E}\!\prod_{j=1}^{s}\Delta_{(i_{j})}(x)\;-\;\mathbb{E}\!\prod_{j=1}^{s}\widetilde{\Delta}_{(i_{j})}(x)\biggr|\;\leq\;K_{1}(x)\,(\eta^{\alpha+1}+\eta\rho^{\beta+1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\prod_{j=1}^{\alpha+1}\bigl|\Delta_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\;\leq\;K_{1}(x)\,(\eta^{\alpha+1}+\eta\rho^{\beta+1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.664em;" width="0.664em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\prod_{j=1}^{\alpha+1}\bigl|\Delta_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\;\leq\;K_{1}(x)\,(\eta^{\alpha+1}+\eta\rho^{\beta+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2m</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-moment of </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is uniformly bounded in </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, i.e. there exists </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{2}\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{2}\in G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, independent of </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl\|x_{k}\bigr\|^{2m}\leq K_{2}(x),\quad k=0,1,\dots,N." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl\|x_{k}\bigr\|^{2m}\leq K_{2}(x),\quad k=0,1,\dots,N.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for each <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G^{\alpha+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G^{\alpha+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a constant <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta,\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta,\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\bigl|\mathbb{E}\,g(x_{k})\;-\;\mathbb{E}\,g(X_{k\eta})\bigr|\;\leq\;C\,(\eta^{\alpha}+\rho^{\beta+1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\bigl|\mathbb{E}\,g(x_{k})\;-\;\mathbb{E}\,g(X_{k\eta})\bigr|\;\leq\;C\,(\eta^{\alpha}+\rho^{\beta+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">By substituting Assumption (i) in the penultimate step of the proof in Theorem 3 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., (2019)</a></cite> with Assumption (i) of our Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem A.2. ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, the same argument goes through and yields the desired conclusion. Hence, we omit the proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we state the key lemma for the two-parameter weak approximation. By employing a Dynkin expansion (see, e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Evans, (2012)</a></cite>) instead of a full Itô–Taylor expansion, it avoids the proliferation of terms and provides a streamlined approach to controlling the remainder error in the two-parameter setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Two-parameter Dynkin (semigroup) expansion)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\in G^{2\alpha+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\in G^{2\alpha+2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and suppose the drift admits the expansion</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(x,\rho)=\sum_{m=0}^{\beta}\rho^{m}\,b_{m}(x)\;+\;O(\eta\rho^{\beta+1}),\qquad\sigma(x)=\sigma_{0}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>β</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(x,\rho)=\sum_{m=0}^{\beta}\rho^{m}\,b_{m}(x)\;+\;O(\eta\rho^{\beta+1}),\qquad\sigma(x)=\sigma_{0}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m}\,\psi(x):=b^{(i)}_{m}(x)\,\partial_{i}\psi(x)\quad(m=0,1,\dots,\beta),\qquad A_{\Delta}\,\psi(x):=\tfrac{1}{2}\,\bigl[\sigma_{0}\sigma_{0}^{T}\bigr]^{(ij)}\,\partial^{2}_{ij}\psi(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m}\,\psi(x):=b^{(i)}_{m}(x)\,\partial_{i}\psi(x)\quad(m=0,1,\dots,\beta),\qquad A_{\Delta}\,\psi(x):=\tfrac{1}{2}\,\bigl[\sigma_{0}\sigma_{0}^{T}\bigr]^{(ij)}\,\partial^{2}_{ij}\psi(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose further that <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{m}\,(m=0,1,\dots,\beta),\sigma_{0}\in G^{2\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{m}\,(m=0,1,\dots,\beta),\sigma_{0}\in G^{2\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, then for any nonnegative integers <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\psi(X_{\eta})\bigr]=\sum_{n=0}^{\alpha}\frac{\eta^{n}}{n!}\sum_{m=0}^{\beta}\rho^{m}\;\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in\{0,\Delta,1,\dots,\beta\}^{n}\\
|\ell|=m\end{subarray}}A_{\ell_{1}}A_{\ell_{2}}\cdots A_{\ell_{n}}\psi(x)\;+\;O(\eta^{\alpha+1})\;+\;O(\eta\rho^{\beta+1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>α</mi></munderover><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>β</mi></munderover><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\psi(X_{\eta})\bigr]=\sum_{n=0}^{\alpha}\frac{\eta^{n}}{n!}\sum_{m=0}^{\beta}\rho^{m}\;\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in\{0,\Delta,1,\dots,\beta\}^{n}\\
|\ell|=m\end{subarray}}A_{\ell_{1}}A_{\ell_{2}}\cdots A_{\ell_{n}}\psi(x)\;+\;O(\eta^{\alpha+1})\;+\;O(\eta\rho^{\beta+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Here <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\ell|:=\sum_{i:\,\ell_{i}\notin\{0,\Delta\}}\ell_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\ell|:=\sum_{i:\,\ell_{i}\notin\{0,\Delta\}}\ell_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and each multi-index
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=(\ell_{1},\dots,\ell_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=(\ell_{1},\dots,\ell_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>
contributes a factor
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{|\ell|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{|\ell|}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and indices <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}=\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}=\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> contribute no <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-power (via <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\;\phi(x)\;=\;\bigl(b(x,\rho)\cdot\nabla\phi\bigr)(x)\;+\;\tfrac{1}{2}\,[\sigma_{0}\sigma_{0}^{T}]^{(ij)}(x)\,\partial_{ij}^{2}\phi(x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\;\phi(x)\;=\;\bigl(b(x,\rho)\cdot\nabla\phi\bigr)(x)\;+\;\tfrac{1}{2}\,[\sigma_{0}\sigma_{0}^{T}]^{(ij)}(x)\,\partial_{ij}^{2}\phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">be the infinitesimal generator of the diffusion. Since</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(x,\rho)=\sum_{m=0}^{\beta}\rho^{m}\,b_{m}(x)+O(\eta\rho^{\beta+1})\;," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>β</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(x,\rho)=\sum_{m=0}^{\beta}\rho^{m}\,b_{m}(x)+O(\eta\rho^{\beta+1})\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">we may write</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=\sum_{m=0}^{\beta}\rho^{m}\,A_{m}\;+A_{\Delta}\;+\;O(\eta\rho^{\beta+1})\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>β</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=\sum_{m=0}^{\beta}\rho^{m}\,A_{m}\;+A_{\Delta}\;+\;O(\eta\rho^{\beta+1})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> are as in the statement. By Dynkin’s formula (or equivalently the semigroup expansion),</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\psi(X_{\eta})\bigr]=\Bigl(e^{\eta L}\psi\Bigr)(x)=\sum_{n=0}^{\alpha}\frac{\eta^{n}}{n!}\,L^{n}\psi(x)\;+\;O(\eta^{\alpha+1})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>α</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\psi(X_{\eta})\bigr]=\Bigl(e^{\eta L}\psi\Bigr)(x)=\sum_{n=0}^{\alpha}\frac{\eta^{n}}{n!}\,L^{n}\psi(x)\;+\;O(\eta^{\alpha+1})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to expand each power <math id="A1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the multinomial theorem,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L^{n}=\bigl(\sum_{m=0}^{\beta}\rho^{m}A_{m}+A_{\Delta}+O(\rho^{\beta+1})\bigr)^{n}=\sum_{m=0}^{\beta}\rho^{m}\!\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in\{0,\Delta,1,\dots,\beta\}^{n}\\
|\ell|=m\end{subarray}}A_{\ell_{1}}A_{\ell_{2}}\cdots A_{\ell_{n}}\;+\;O(\rho^{\beta+1})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>β</mi></munderover><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>β</mi></munderover><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{n}=\bigl(\sum_{m=0}^{\beta}\rho^{m}A_{m}+A_{\Delta}+O(\rho^{\beta+1})\bigr)^{n}=\sum_{m=0}^{\beta}\rho^{m}\!\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in\{0,\Delta,1,\dots,\beta\}^{n}\\
|\ell|=m\end{subarray}}A_{\ell_{1}}A_{\ell_{2}}\cdots A_{\ell_{n}}\;+\;O(\rho^{\beta+1})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\eta^{n}}{n!}\,L^{n}\psi(x)=\frac{\eta^{n}}{n!}\sum_{m=0}^{\beta}\rho^{m}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in\{0,\Delta,1,\dots,\beta\}^{n}\\
|\ell|=m\end{subarray}}A_{\ell_{1}}A_{\ell_{2}}\cdots A_{\ell_{n}}\psi(x)\;+\;O(\eta^{n+1})+O(\eta\rho^{\beta+1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>β</mi></munderover><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\eta^{n}}{n!}\,L^{n}\psi(x)=\frac{\eta^{n}}{n!}\sum_{m=0}^{\beta}\rho^{m}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in\{0,\Delta,1,\dots,\beta\}^{n}\\
|\ell|=m\end{subarray}}A_{\ell_{1}}A_{\ell_{2}}\cdots A_{\ell_{n}}\psi(x)\;+\;O(\eta^{n+1})+O(\eta\rho^{\beta+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.7.1" class="ltx_text">Summing over <math id="A1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=0,1,\dots,\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=0,1,\dots,\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and collecting the remainders <math id="A1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\eta^{\alpha+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\eta^{\alpha+1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\eta\rho^{\beta+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\eta\rho^{\beta+1})</annotation></semantics></math>
yields exactly the claimed two-parameter expansion.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Since our focus in this paper is on the order-(1,1) weak approximation, we now present the one-step approximation lemma for SDEs in the case <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>, as follows. For readers interested in higher-order two-parameter weak approximations, it is sufficient to apply higher-order truncations of the Dynkin and Taylor expansions in the two lemmas below and then match the corresponding moments at each order.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(One-step moment estimates up to <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{1},\rho^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{1},\rho^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for SDEs)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the drift admits the expansion</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(x,\rho)=b_{0}(x)+\rho\,b_{1}(x)+O(\rho^{2}),\qquad\sigma(x)=\sigma_{0}(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(x,\rho)=b_{0}(x)+\rho\,b_{1}(x)+O(\rho^{2}),\qquad\sigma(x)=\sigma_{0}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and assume <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0},b_{1},\sigma_{0}\in G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0},b_{1},\sigma_{0}\in G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\Delta}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\Delta}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the one-step increment defined in (<a href="#A1.E24" title="In Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>). Then:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\widetilde{\Delta}_{(i)}(x)]=\eta\bigl(b^{(i)}_{0}(x)+\rho\,b^{(i)}_{1}(x)\bigr)+O(\eta^{2})+O(\eta\,\rho^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\widetilde{\Delta}_{(i)}(x)]=\eta\bigl(b^{(i)}_{0}(x)+\rho\,b^{(i)}_{1}(x)\bigr)+O(\eta^{2})+O(\eta\,\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\widetilde{\Delta}_{(i)}(x)\,\widetilde{\Delta}_{(j)}(x)\bigr]=\eta^{2}\bigl(b_{0}^{(i)}(x)\,b_{0}^{(j)}(x)\;+\;\sum_{k}\sigma_{0}^{(i,k)}(x)\,\sigma_{0}^{(j,k)}(x)\bigr)\;+\;\eta^{2}\rho\bigl(b_{0}^{(i)}(x)\,b_{1}^{(j)}(x)\;+\;b_{1}^{(i)}(x)\,b_{0}^{(j)}(x)\bigr)+\;O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2})\;+\;O(\eta^{3})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\widetilde{\Delta}_{(i)}(x)\,\widetilde{\Delta}_{(j)}(x)\bigr]=\eta^{2}\bigl(b_{0}^{(i)}(x)\,b_{0}^{(j)}(x)\;+\;\sum_{k}\sigma_{0}^{(i,k)}(x)\,\sigma_{0}^{(j,k)}(x)\bigr)\;+\;\eta^{2}\rho\bigl(b_{0}^{(i)}(x)\,b_{1}^{(j)}(x)\;+\;b_{1}^{(i)}(x)\,b_{0}^{(j)}(x)\bigr)+\;O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2})\;+\;O(\eta^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\Bigl[\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl|\widetilde{\Delta}_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\Bigr]=O(\eta^{3})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\Bigl[\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl|\widetilde{\Delta}_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\Bigr]=O(\eta^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1,2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1,2,3</annotation></semantics></math> and any choice of indices <math id="A1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{1},\dots,i_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{1},\dots,i_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the test function</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{s}(z)\;=\;\prod_{j=1}^{s}\bigl(z_{(i_{j})}-x_{(i_{j})}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{s}(z)\;=\;\prod_{j=1}^{s}\bigl(z_{(i_{j})}-x_{(i_{j})}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{s}\in C^{4}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{s}\in C^{4}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> with at most polynomial growth, we may invoke Lemma A.2 with truncation orders <math id="A1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\psi(x)\bigr]=\psi(x)+\eta\sum_{\ell\in\{0,\Delta\}}A_{\ell}\psi(x)+\eta\rho\,A_{1}\psi(x)+O(\eta^{2})+O(\eta\rho^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\psi(x)\bigr]=\psi(x)+\eta\sum_{\ell\in\{0,\Delta\}}A_{\ell}\psi(x)+\eta\rho\,A_{1}\psi(x)+O(\eta^{2})+O(\eta\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">(i) <em id="A1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">First moment.</em>
Here</p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{1}(z)=z_{(i)}-x_{(i)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{1}(z)=z_{(i)}-x_{(i)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p10.2" class="ltx_p">Hence</p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\widetilde{\Delta}_{(i)}(x)]=\eta\,b_{0}^{(i)}(x)\;+\;\eta\,\rho\,b_{1}^{(i)}(x)\;+\;O(\eta^{2})\;+\;O(\eta\,\rho^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\widetilde{\Delta}_{(i)}(x)]=\eta\,b_{0}^{(i)}(x)\;+\;\eta\,\rho\,b_{1}^{(i)}(x)\;+\;O(\eta^{2})\;+\;O(\eta\,\rho^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p10.3" class="ltx_p">proving (i).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">(ii) <em id="A1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Second moment.</em>
Now</p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{2}(z)=(z_{(i)}-x_{(i)})(z_{(j)}-x_{(j)})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{2}(z)=(z_{(i)}-x_{(i)})(z_{(j)}-x_{(j)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p11.2" class="ltx_p">It follows that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\widetilde{\Delta}_{(i)}(x)\,\widetilde{\Delta}_{(j)}(x)\bigr]=\eta^{2}\Bigl[b_{0}^{(i)}b_{0}^{(j)}\;+\;\sum_{k}\sigma_{0}^{(i,k)}\sigma_{0}^{(j,k)}\Bigr]+\eta^{2}\rho\bigl[b_{0}^{(i)}b_{1}^{(j)}+b_{1}^{(i)}b_{0}^{(j)}\bigr]+O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2})\;+\;O(\eta^{3})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.335em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\widetilde{\Delta}_{(i)}(x)\,\widetilde{\Delta}_{(j)}(x)\bigr]=\eta^{2}\Bigl[b_{0}^{(i)}b_{0}^{(j)}\;+\;\sum_{k}\sigma_{0}^{(i,k)}\sigma_{0}^{(j,k)}\Bigr]+\eta^{2}\rho\bigl[b_{0}^{(i)}b_{1}^{(j)}+b_{1}^{(i)}b_{0}^{(j)}\bigr]+O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2})\;+\;O(\eta^{3}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p11.3" class="ltx_p">proving (ii).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">(iii) <em id="A1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Third moment.</em>
Finally,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{3}(z)=\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl(z_{(i_{j})}-x_{(i_{j})}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{3}(z)=\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl(z_{(i_{j})}-x_{(i_{j})}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p12.2" class="ltx_p">and since each nonzero term in the expansion has total order <math id="A1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma A.2 gives</p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\Bigl[\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl|\widetilde{\Delta}_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\Bigr]=\mathbb{E}\bigl[|\psi_{3}(X_{k+1})|\bigr]=O(\eta^{3})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\Bigl[\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl|\widetilde{\Delta}_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\Bigr]=\mathbb{E}\bigl[|\psi_{3}(X_{k+1})|\bigr]=O(\eta^{3}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p12.3" class="ltx_p">establishing (iii). This completes the proof.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to the continuous-time setting, we require the following one-step error lemma for the discrete algorithm in the case <math id="A1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.5</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(One-step moment estimates up to <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{1},\rho^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{1},\rho^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for the discrete algorithm)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the discrete update <a href="#A1.E22" title="In Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a> admits the expansion</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(x,\gamma,\rho)=h_{0}(x,\gamma)+\rho\,h_{1}(x,\gamma)+O(\rho^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x,\gamma,\rho)=h_{0}(x,\gamma)+\rho\,h_{1}(x,\gamma)+O(\rho^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and assume <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0},h_{1}\in G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0},h_{1}\in G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the one-step increment defined in (<a href="#A1.E24" title="In Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>). Then:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{(i)}(x)]=\eta h^{(i)}_{0}(x)+\eta\rho\,h^{(i)}_{1}(x)+O(\eta\,\rho^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{(i)}(x)]=\eta h^{(i)}_{0}(x)+\eta\rho\,h^{(i)}_{1}(x)+O(\eta\,\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\,\Delta_{(j)}(x)\bigr]=\eta^{2}\bigl(h_{0}^{(i)}(x)\,h_{0}^{(j)}(x)+\Sigma_{0,0}^{(ij)}(x)\bigr)+\eta^{2}\rho\bigl(h_{0}^{(i)}(x)\,h_{1}^{(j)}(x)\;+\;h_{1}^{(i)}(x)\,h_{0}^{(j)}(x)+\Sigma_{0,1}^{(ij)}(x)+\Sigma_{1,0}^{(ij)}(x)\bigr)+\;O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\,\Delta_{(j)}(x)\bigr]=\eta^{2}\bigl(h_{0}^{(i)}(x)\,h_{0}^{(j)}(x)+\Sigma_{0,0}^{(ij)}(x)\bigr)+\eta^{2}\rho\bigl(h_{0}^{(i)}(x)\,h_{1}^{(j)}(x)\;+\;h_{1}^{(i)}(x)\,h_{0}^{(j)}(x)+\Sigma_{0,1}^{(ij)}(x)+\Sigma_{1,0}^{(ij)}(x)\bigr)+\;O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\Bigl[\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl|\Delta_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\Bigr]=O(\eta^{3})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\Bigl[\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl|\Delta_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\Bigr]=O(\eta^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0}(x)=\mathbb{E}h_{0}(x,\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}(x)=\mathbb{E}h_{0}(x,\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1}(x)=\mathbb{E}h_{1}(x,\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1}(x)=\mathbb{E}h_{1}(x,\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{0,0}(x)=\Cov(h_{0}(x,\gamma),h_{0}(x,\gamma))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{0,0}(x)=\Cov(h_{0}(x,\gamma),h_{0}(x,\gamma))</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{0,1}(x)=\Cov(h_{0}(x,\gamma),h_{1}(x,\gamma))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{0,1}(x)=\Cov(h_{0}(x,\gamma),h_{1}(x,\gamma)).</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(x)\;=\;\eta\,h(x,\gamma,\rho)\;=\;\eta\bigl(h_{0}(x,\gamma)+\rho\,h_{1}(x,\gamma)+O(\rho^{2})\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(x)\;=\;\eta\,h(x,\gamma,\rho)\;=\;\eta\bigl(h_{0}(x,\gamma)+\rho\,h_{1}(x,\gamma)+O(\rho^{2})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence for each coordinate <math id="A1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p15.1" class="ltx_p">(i) <em id="A1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">First moment.</em></p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex32X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{(i)}(x)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{(i)}(x)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[h_{0}^{(i)}(x,\gamma)+\rho\,h_{1}^{(i)}(x,\gamma)+O(\rho^{2})\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[h_{0}^{(i)}(x,\gamma)+\rho\,h_{1}^{(i)}(x,\gamma)+O(\rho^{2})\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex32Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta\bigl(h_{0}^{(i)}(x)+\rho\,h_{1}^{(i)}(x)\bigr)+\;O(\eta\,\rho^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta\bigl(h_{0}^{(i)}(x)+\rho\,h_{1}^{(i)}(x)\bigr)+\;O(\eta\,\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">(ii) <em id="A1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Second moment.</em></p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex33X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\,\Delta_{(j)}(x)\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\,\Delta_{(j)}(x)\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta^{2}\,\mathbb{E}_{\gamma}\Bigl[\bigl(h_{0}^{(i)}(x,\gamma)+\rho\,h_{1}^{(i)}(x,\gamma)\bigr)\bigl(h_{0}^{(j)}(x,\gamma)+\rho\,h_{1}^{(j)}(x,\gamma)\bigr)\Bigr]+O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta^{2}\,\mathbb{E}_{\gamma}\Bigl[\bigl(h_{0}^{(i)}(x,\gamma)+\rho\,h_{1}^{(i)}(x,\gamma)\bigr)\bigl(h_{0}^{(j)}(x,\gamma)+\rho\,h_{1}^{(j)}(x,\gamma)\bigr)\Bigr]+O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex33Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta^{2}\Bigl\{\mathbb{E}_{\gamma}\bigl[h_{0}^{(i)}(x,\gamma)\,h_{0}^{(j)}(x,\gamma)\bigr]+\rho\,\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{\gamma}[h_{0}^{(i)}(x,\gamma)\,h_{1}^{(j)}(x,\gamma)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>η</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta^{2}\Bigl\{\mathbb{E}_{\gamma}\bigl[h_{0}^{(i)}(x,\gamma)\,h_{0}^{(j)}(x,\gamma)\bigr]+\rho\,\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{\gamma}[h_{0}^{(i)}(x,\gamma)\,h_{1}^{(j)}(x,\gamma)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex33Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}_{\gamma}[h_{1}^{(i)}(x,\gamma)\,h_{0}^{(j)}(x,\gamma)]\bigr)\Bigr\}+O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}_{\gamma}[h_{1}^{(i)}(x,\gamma)\,h_{0}^{(j)}(x,\gamma)]\bigr)\Bigr\}+O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex33Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta^{2}\Bigl\{h_{0}^{(i)}(x)\,h_{0}^{(j)}(x)+\Sigma_{0,0}^{(ij)}(x)\Bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta^{2}\Bigl\{h_{0}^{(i)}(x)\,h_{0}^{(j)}(x)+\Sigma_{0,0}^{(ij)}(x)\Bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex33Xd"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\;\eta^{2}\rho\Bigl\{h_{0}^{(i)}(x)\,h_{1}^{(j)}(x)+h_{1}^{(i)}(x)\,h_{0}^{(j)}(x)+\Sigma_{0,1}^{(ij)}(x)+\Sigma_{1,0}^{(ij)}(x)\Bigr\}+O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\;\eta^{2}\rho\Bigl\{h_{0}^{(i)}(x)\,h_{1}^{(j)}(x)+h_{1}^{(i)}(x)\,h_{0}^{(j)}(x)+\Sigma_{0,1}^{(ij)}(x)+\Sigma_{1,0}^{(ij)}(x)\Bigr\}+O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p17.1" class="ltx_p">(iii) <em id="A1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Third moment.</em>
Since <math id="A1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0},h_{1}\in G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0},h_{1}\in G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> implies that all moments up to order three are finite and <math id="A1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=O(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=O(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\bigl|\Delta_{(i_{1})}\Delta_{(i_{2})}\Delta_{(i_{3})}\bigr|\Bigr]=O(\eta^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\bigl|\Delta_{(i_{1})}\Delta_{(i_{2})}\Delta_{(i_{3})}\bigr|\Bigr]=O(\eta^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p17.2" class="ltx_p">This completes the proof.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>SDE approximation for USAM variants</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that the update rules of USAM variants are defined by:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{mini-batch USAM:}\quad x_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>mini-batch USAM:</mtext><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{mini-batch USAM:}\quad x_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{k}-\eta\,\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}(x_{k})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{k}-\eta\,\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}(x_{k})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{n-USAM:}\quad x_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>n-USAM:</mtext><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{n-USAM:}\quad x_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{k}-\eta\,\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\nabla f(x_{k})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{k}-\eta\,\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\nabla f(x_{k})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{m-USAM:}\quad x_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>m-USAM:</mtext><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{m-USAM:}\quad x_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{k}-\frac{\eta\,m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{k}-\frac{\eta\,m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we impose the following growth assumption on the functions <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The functions <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> belong to the class <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Mini-batch USAM</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the mini-batch USAM algorithm (<a href="#A2.E25" title="In Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>), we define the continuous-time approximation <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as the solution to the following SDE:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle dX_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle dX_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\nabla f^{USAM}(X_{t})\,dt+\sqrt{\eta\,\Sigma^{USAM}(X_{t})}\,dW_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\nabla f^{USAM}(X_{t})\,dt+\sqrt{\eta\,\Sigma^{USAM}(X_{t})}\,dW_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{USAM}(X_{t}):=f(X_{t})+\frac{\rho}{2}\|\nabla f(X_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\rho}{2|\gamma|}\mathrm{tr}(V(X_{t}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{USAM}(X_{t}):=f(X_{t})+\frac{\rho}{2}\|\nabla f(X_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\rho}{2|\gamma|}\mathrm{tr}(V(X_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{USAM}(X_{t}):=\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t})+\rho\bigl(\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})+\Sigma_{0,1}^{\top}(X_{t})\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{USAM}(X_{t}):=\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t})+\rho\bigl(\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})+\Sigma_{0,1}^{\top}(X_{t})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\left[\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)^{\top}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\left[\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t}))\cdot\bigl(\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(X_{t})\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\mathbb{E}[\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(X_{t})\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})]\bigr)^{\top}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t}))\cdot\bigl(\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(X_{t})\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\mathbb{E}[\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(X_{t})\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})]\bigr)^{\top}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(mini-batch USAM SDE, adapted from Theorem 3.2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Compagnoni et al., (2023)</a></cite>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Notation and assumption ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote by <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> the mini-batch USAM iterates in (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.3 SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), and let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{t}\}_{t\in[0,T]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{t}\}_{t\in[0,T]}</annotation></semantics></math> be the solution of the SDE (<a href="#A2.E28" title="In B.1 Mini-batch USAM ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>). Suppose:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The functions</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f^{\mathrm{USAM}}\;=\;\nabla\Bigl(f+\frac{\rho}{2}\|\nabla f\|^{2}+\frac{\rho}{2|\gamma|}\mathrm{tr}(V)\Bigr)\quad\text{and}\quad\sqrt{\Sigma^{\mathrm{USAM}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>USAM</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>USAM</mi></msup></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f^{\mathrm{USAM}}\;=\;\nabla\Bigl(f+\frac{\rho}{2}\|\nabla f\|^{2}+\frac{\rho}{2|\gamma|}\mathrm{tr}(V)\Bigr)\quad\text{and}\quad\sqrt{\Sigma^{\mathrm{USAM}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">are Lipschitz on </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The mapping</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{\gamma}(x)\;=\;-\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.058em">=</mo><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\gamma}(x)\;=\;-\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfies, almost surely, the Lipschitz condition</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla h_{\gamma}(x)-\nabla h_{\gamma}(y)\|\;\leq\;L_{\gamma}\,\|x-y\|,\qquad\forall\,x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla h_{\gamma}(x)-\nabla h_{\gamma}(y)\|\;\leq\;L_{\gamma}\,\|x-y\|,\qquad\forall\,x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\gamma}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\gamma}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> a.s. and </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[L_{\gamma}^{m}]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[L_{\gamma}^{m}]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for every </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{t}:t\in[0,T]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{t}:t\in[0,T]\}</annotation></semantics></math> is an order-<math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math> weak approximation of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, namely: for each <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a constant <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta,\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta,\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\Bigl|\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(x_{k})\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(X_{k\eta})\bigr]\Bigr|\;\leq\;C\,\bigl(\eta+\rho^{2}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\Bigl|\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(x_{k})\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(X_{k\eta})\bigr]\Bigr|\;\leq\;C\,\bigl(\eta+\rho^{2}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof Sketch.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem B.2 (mini-batch USAM SDE, adapted from Theorem 3.2 of ( ) ). ‣ B.1 Mini-batch USAM ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> follows by replacing the single-parameter Lemmas A.1, A.2 and A.5 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Compagnoni et al., (2023)</a></cite> with our two-parameter versions—Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem A.2. ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for SDEs). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for the discrete algorithm). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>—imposing the extra global Lipschitz conditions to guarantee existence and uniqueness of the strong solution, and using our Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Notation and assumption ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> to expand the drift term. We therefore omit the routine algebraic details.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>n-USAM</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the n-USAM algorithm, we define the continuous-time approximation <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as the solution to the following SDE:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle dX_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle dX_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\nabla f^{n\text{-}USAM}(X_{t})\,dt+\sqrt{\eta\,\Sigma^{n\text{-}USAM}(X_{t})}\,dW_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\nabla f^{n\text{-}USAM}(X_{t})\,dt+\sqrt{\eta\,\Sigma^{n\text{-}USAM}(X_{t})}\,dW_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{n\text{-}USAM}(X_{t}):=f(X_{t})+\frac{\rho}{2}\|\nabla f(X_{t})\|^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{n\text{-}USAM}(X_{t}):=f(X_{t})+\frac{\rho}{2}\|\nabla f(X_{t})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{n\text{-}USAM}(X_{t}):=\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t})+\rho\bigl(\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})+\Sigma_{0,1}^{\top}(X_{t})\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{n\text{-}USAM}(X_{t}):=\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t})+\rho\bigl(\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})+\Sigma_{0,1}^{\top}(X_{t})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\left[\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)^{\top}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\left[\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t}))\cdot\bigl((\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla^{2}f(X_{t}))\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)^{\top}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t}))\cdot\bigl((\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla^{2}f(X_{t}))\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)^{\top}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by deriving, via the following lemma, a one-step error estimate for the n-USAM discrete algorithm, which will be used to prove the main approximation theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(One-step moment estimates for n-USAM up to <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{1},\rho^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{1},\rho^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Notation and assumption ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>. Define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{i}f^{\mathrm{n\text{-}USAM}}(x):=\partial_{i}f(x)\;+\;\rho\sum_{j}\partial^{2}_{ij}f(x)\,\partial_{j}f(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>USAM</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{i}f^{\mathrm{n\text{-}USAM}}(x):=\partial_{i}f(x)\;+\;\rho\sum_{j}\partial^{2}_{ij}f(x)\,\partial_{j}f(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the one-step increment defined in (<a href="#A1.E24" title="In Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>). Then:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\bigr]=-\,\partial_{i}f^{\mathrm{n\text{-}USAM}}(x)\,\eta+O(\eta\,\rho^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>USAM</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\bigr]=-\,\partial_{i}f^{\mathrm{n\text{-}USAM}}(x)\,\eta+O(\eta\,\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\,\Delta_{(j)}(x)\bigr]=\eta^{2}\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\,\partial_{j}f(x)+\;\Sigma^{\mathrm{n\text{-}USAM}}_{(ij)}(x)\Bigr)+\eta^{2}\rho\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{jl}f(x)\,\partial_{l}f(x)+\partial_{j}f(x)\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{il}f(x)\,\partial_{l}f(x)\Bigr)+O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>USAM</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\,\Delta_{(j)}(x)\bigr]=\eta^{2}\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\,\partial_{j}f(x)+\;\Sigma^{\mathrm{n\text{-}USAM}}_{(ij)}(x)\Bigr)+\eta^{2}\rho\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{jl}f(x)\,\partial_{l}f(x)+\partial_{j}f(x)\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{il}f(x)\,\partial_{l}f(x)\Bigr)+O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl|\Delta_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\Bigr]=O(\eta^{3})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl|\Delta_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\Bigr]=O(\eta^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that the n-USAM update is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{k+1}=x_{k}\;-\;\eta\,\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\nabla f(x_{k})\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k+1}=x_{k}\;-\;\eta\,\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\nabla f(x_{k})\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">so the one-step increment</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(x)\;=\;x_{k+1}-x_{k}=\eta h(x,\gamma,\rho)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(x)\;=\;x_{k+1}-x_{k}=\eta h(x,\gamma,\rho),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h(x,\gamma,\rho):=-\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,\nabla f(x)\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x,\gamma,\rho):=-\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,\nabla f(x)\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">By Taylor’s theorem with integral remainder <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Folland,, 2005</a>)</cite> we have, for each <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,\nabla f(x)\bigr)=\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)+\rho\,\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(x)\,\nabla f(x)+R(x,\gamma,\rho)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,\nabla f(x)\bigr)=\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)+\rho\,\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(x)\,\nabla f(x)+R(x,\gamma,\rho),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R(x,\gamma,\rho)=\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\;D^{3}f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+t\,\rho\,\nabla f(x)\bigr)\bigl[\rho\,\nabla f(x),\,\rho\,\nabla f(x)\bigr]\,dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(x,\gamma,\rho)=\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\;D^{3}f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+t\,\rho\,\nabla f(x)\bigr)\bigl[\rho\,\nabla f(x),\,\rho\,\nabla f(x)\bigr]\,dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{3}f_{\gamma}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{3}f_{\gamma}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the third-order tensor of partial derivatives of <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{3}f_{\gamma}(y)[u,v]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{3}f_{\gamma}(y)[u,v]</annotation></semantics></math> its bilinear action on vectors <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma}\in G^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma}\in G^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a polynomially bounded function <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(x)\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(x)\in G</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\|D^{3}f_{\gamma}(y)\bigr\|\;\leq\;K(x),\quad\forall\,y\;\text{with}\;\|y-x\|\leq\rho\,\|\nabla f(x)\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>with</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\|D^{3}f_{\gamma}(y)\bigr\|\;\leq\;K(x),\quad\forall\,y\;\text{with}\;\|y-x\|\leq\rho\,\|\nabla f(x)\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bigl\|R(x,\gamma,\rho)\bigr\|\;\leq\;\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\,\bigl\|D^{3}f_{\gamma}(x+t\rho\nabla f(x))\bigr\|\,\bigl\|\rho\nabla f(x)\bigr\|^{2}\,dt\;\leq\;K(x)\,\frac{\rho^{2}}{2}\,\|\nabla f(x)\|^{2}=O\bigl(\rho^{2}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.169em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.391em">≤</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.059em">∥</mo><mo mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\|R(x,\gamma,\rho)\bigr\|\;\leq\;\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\,\bigl\|D^{3}f_{\gamma}(x+t\rho\nabla f(x))\bigr\|\,\bigl\|\rho\nabla f(x)\bigr\|^{2}\,dt\;\leq\;K(x)\,\frac{\rho^{2}}{2}\,\|\nabla f(x)\|^{2}=O\bigl(\rho^{2}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">uniformly in <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Accordingly, a Taylor expansion in <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla f_{\gamma}(x+\rho\nabla f(x))=\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)+\rho\,\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(x)\,\nabla f(x)+O(\rho^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f_{\gamma}(x+\rho\nabla f(x))=\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)+\rho\,\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(x)\,\nabla f(x)+O(\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(x,\gamma,\rho)=h_{0}(x,\gamma)\;+\;\rho\,h_{1}(x,\gamma)\;+\;O(\rho^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x,\gamma,\rho)=h_{0}(x,\gamma)\;+\;\rho\,h_{1}(x,\gamma)\;+\;O(\rho^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">with</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{0}(x,\gamma):=-\nabla f_{\gamma}(x),\qquad h_{1}(x,\gamma):=-\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(x)\,\nabla f(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}(x,\gamma):=-\nabla f_{\gamma}(x),\qquad h_{1}(x,\gamma):=-\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(x)\,\nabla f(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Notation and assumption ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, each <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0},h_{1}\in G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0},h_{1}\in G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[h_{0}(x,\gamma)]=-\nabla f(x),\quad\mathbb{E}[h_{1}(x,\gamma)]=-\nabla^{2}f(x)\,\nabla f(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[h_{0}(x,\gamma)]=-\nabla f(x),\quad\mathbb{E}[h_{1}(x,\gamma)]=-\nabla^{2}f(x)\,\nabla f(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">We may therefore apply Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for the discrete algorithm). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a> with these
<math id="A2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0},h_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0},h_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which yields exactly the three moment expansions up to
<math id="A2.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{1},\rho^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{1},\rho^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3 (One-step moment estimates for n-USAM up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1). ‣ B.2 n-USAM ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, we derived one-step moment estimates for the n-USAM discrete algorithm and, via Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for SDEs). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, for its corresponding SDE update (<a href="#A2.E26" title="In Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>). These estimates demonstrate that the first- and second-order moments satisfy the matching conditions of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem A.2. ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>. Together with the uniform moment bounds from Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ Appendix D Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, we are now ready to establish the main weak-approximation theorem for n-USAM.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(n-USAM SDE)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Notation and assumption ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote by <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> the n-USAM iterates in (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), and let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{t}\}_{t\in[0,T]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{t}\}_{t\in[0,T]}</annotation></semantics></math> be the solution of the SDE (<a href="#A2.E30" title="In B.2 n-USAM ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>). Suppose:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The functions</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f^{\mathrm{n\text{-}USAM}}\;=\;\nabla\Bigl(f+\tfrac{\rho}{2}\|\nabla f\|^{2}\Bigr)\quad\text{and}\quad\sqrt{\Sigma^{\mathrm{n\text{-}USAM}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>USAM</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>USAM</mi></mrow></msup></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f^{\mathrm{n\text{-}USAM}}\;=\;\nabla\Bigl(f+\tfrac{\rho}{2}\|\nabla f\|^{2}\Bigr)\quad\text{and}\quad\sqrt{\Sigma^{\mathrm{n\text{-}USAM}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">are Lipschitz on </span><math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The mapping</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{\gamma}(x)\;=\;-\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,\nabla f(x)\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.058em">=</mo><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\gamma}(x)\;=\;-\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,\nabla f(x)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfies, almost surely, the Lipschitz condition</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla h_{\gamma}(x)-\nabla h_{\gamma}(y)\|\;\leq\;L_{\gamma}\,\|x-y\|,\qquad\forall\,x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla h_{\gamma}(x)-\nabla h_{\gamma}(y)\|\;\leq\;L_{\gamma}\,\|x-y\|,\qquad\forall\,x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\gamma}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\gamma}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> a.s. and </span><math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[L_{\gamma}^{m}]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[L_{\gamma}^{m}]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for every </span><math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{t}:t\in[0,T]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{t}:t\in[0,T]\}</annotation></semantics></math> is an order-<math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math> weak approximation of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, namely: for each <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a constant <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta,\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta,\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\Bigl|\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(x_{k})\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(X_{k\eta})\bigr]\Bigr|\;\leq\;C\,\bigl(\eta+\rho^{2}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\Bigl|\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(x_{k})\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(X_{k\eta})\bigr]\Bigr|\;\leq\;C\,\bigl(\eta+\rho^{2}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we verify that SDE (<a href="#A2.E30" title="In B.2 n-USAM ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) admits a unique strong solution.
By assumption, both the drift and diffusion coefficients are globally Lipschitz, which in turn implies a linear-growth condition.
Therefore, Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1 (Existence and Uniqueness of Strong Solutions ( , )). ‣ Appendix D Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> applies and yields the existence and uniqueness of a strong solution on <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, by Lemmas <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for SDEs). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3 (One-step moment estimates for n-USAM up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1). ‣ B.2 n-USAM ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, and <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ Appendix D Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, all the conditions of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem A.2. ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> are satisfied, and the proof is complete.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark B.5</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Lipschitz conditions are to ensure that the SDE has a unique strong solution with uniformly bounded moments. It is possible to appropriately relax them if we allow weak solutions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mil’shtein,, 1986</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>m-USAM</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the m-USAM algorithm, we define the continuous-time approximation <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as the solution to the following SDE:</p>
<table id="A2.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="dX_{t}=-\nabla\bigl(f(X_{t})+\frac{\rho}{2}\|\nabla f(X_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\rho}{2m}\mathrm{tr}(V(X_{t}))\bigr)dt+\sqrt{\frac{m\eta}{|\gamma|}\Sigma^{m-USAM}(X_{t})}dW_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dX_{t}=-\nabla\bigl(f(X_{t})+\frac{\rho}{2}\|\nabla f(X_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\rho}{2m}\mathrm{tr}(V(X_{t}))\bigr)dt+\sqrt{\frac{m\eta}{|\gamma|}\Sigma^{m-USAM}(X_{t})}dW_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A2.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{m-USAM}(X_{t}):=\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t})+\rho(\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})+\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})^{\top})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{m-USAM}(X_{t}):=\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t})+\rho(\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})+\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})^{\top}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\left[\bigl(\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)\bigl(\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)^{\top}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\left[\bigl(\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)\bigl(\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)^{\top}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t}))\cdot\bigl(\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})-\mathbb{E}[\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})]\bigr)^{\top}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t}))\cdot\bigl(\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})-\mathbb{E}[\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})]\bigr)^{\top}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by deriving, via the following lemma, a one-step error estimate for the m-USAM discrete algorithm, which will be used to prove the main approximation theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.6</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(One-step moment estimates for m-USAM up to <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{1},\rho^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{1},\rho^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Notation and assumption ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>. Define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{i}f^{m-USAM}(x):=\partial_{i}f(x)+\rho\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{j=1}^{d}\partial_{ij}^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\partial_{j}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{i}f^{m-USAM}(x):=\partial_{i}f(x)+\rho\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{j=1}^{d}\partial_{ij}^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\partial_{j}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the one-step increment defined in (<a href="#A1.E24" title="In Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>). Then:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\bigr]=-\,\partial_{i}f^{\mathrm{m\text{-}USAM}}(x)\,\eta+O(\eta\,\rho^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>USAM</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\bigr]=-\,\partial_{i}f^{\mathrm{m\text{-}USAM}}(x)\,\eta+O(\eta\,\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\,\Delta_{(j)}(x)\bigr]=\eta^{2}\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\,\partial_{j}f(x)+\;\Sigma^{\mathrm{m\text{-}USAM}}_{(ij)}(x)\Bigr)+\eta^{2}\rho\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{jl}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\,\partial_{l}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)+\partial_{j}f(x)\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{il}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\,\partial_{l}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\Bigr)+O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>USAM</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\,\Delta_{(j)}(x)\bigr]=\eta^{2}\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\,\partial_{j}f(x)+\;\Sigma^{\mathrm{m\text{-}USAM}}_{(ij)}(x)\Bigr)+\eta^{2}\rho\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{jl}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\,\partial_{l}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)+\partial_{j}f(x)\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{il}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\,\partial_{l}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\Bigr)+O(\eta^{2}\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl|\Delta_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\Bigr]=O(\eta^{3})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl|\Delta_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\Bigr]=O(\eta^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that the m-USAM update is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\frac{\eta\,m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\frac{\eta\,m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">so the one-step increment</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(x)\;=\;x_{k+1}-x_{k}=\eta h(x,\gamma,\rho)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(x)\;=\;x_{k+1}-x_{k}=\eta h(x,\gamma,\rho),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h(x,\gamma,\rho):=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x,\gamma,\rho):=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">By Taylor’s theorem with integral remainder <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Folland,, 2005</a>)</cite> we have, for each <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\\
|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\bigr)=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\\
|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})+\rho\,\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})+R(x,\gamma,\rho)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\\
|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\bigr)=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\\
|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})+\rho\,\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})+R(x,\gamma,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R(x,\gamma,\rho)=\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\;D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x+t\,\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\bigr)\bigl[\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x),\,\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\bigr]\,dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(x,\gamma,\rho)=\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\;D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x+t\,\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\bigr)\bigl[\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x),\,\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\bigr]\,dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the third-order tensor of partial derivatives of <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(y)[u,v]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(y)[u,v]</annotation></semantics></math> its bilinear action on vectors <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\in G^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\in G^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a polynomially bounded function <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(x)\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(x)\in G</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\|D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(y)\bigr\|\;\leq\;K(x),\quad\forall\,y\;\text{with}\;\|y-x\|\leq\rho\,\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>with</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\|D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(y)\bigr\|\;\leq\;K(x),\quad\forall\,y\;\text{with}\;\|y-x\|\leq\rho\,\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl\|R(x,\gamma,\rho)\bigr\|\;\leq\;\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\,\bigl\|D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x+t\rho\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x))\bigr\|\,\bigl\|\rho\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\bigr\|^{2}\,dt\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.169em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.059em">∥</mo><mo mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl\|R(x,\gamma,\rho)\bigr\|\;\leq\;\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\,\bigl\|D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x+t\rho\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x))\bigr\|\,\bigl\|\rho\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\bigr\|^{2}\,dt\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex70.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\;K(x)\,\frac{\rho^{2}}{2}\,\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\;K(x)\,\frac{\rho^{2}}{2}\,\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O\bigl(\rho^{2}\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O\bigl(\rho^{2}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">uniformly in <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Accordingly, a Taylor expansion in <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla f_{\gamma}(x+\rho\nabla f(x))=\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)+\rho\,\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(x)\,\nabla f(x)+O(\rho^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f_{\gamma}(x+\rho\nabla f(x))=\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)+\rho\,\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(x)\,\nabla f(x)+O(\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(x,\gamma,\rho)=h_{0}(x,\gamma)\;+\;\rho\,h_{1}(x,\gamma)\;+\;O(\rho^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x,\gamma,\rho)=h_{0}(x,\gamma)\;+\;\rho\,h_{1}(x,\gamma)\;+\;O(\rho^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">with</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{0}(x,\gamma):=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\\
|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k}),\qquad h_{1}(x,\gamma):=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\;\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\\
|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo lspace="0.447em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}(x,\gamma):=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\\
|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k}),\qquad h_{1}(x,\gamma):=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\;\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\\
|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Notation and assumption ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, each <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0},h_{1}\in G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0},h_{1}\in G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[h_{0}(x,\gamma)]=-\nabla f(x),\quad\mathbb{E}[h_{1}(x,\gamma)]=-\mathbb{E}\big[\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[h_{0}(x,\gamma)]=-\nabla f(x),\quad\mathbb{E}[h_{1}(x,\gamma)]=-\mathbb{E}\big[\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">We may therefore apply Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for the discrete algorithm). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a> with these
<math id="A2.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0},h_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0},h_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which yields exactly the three moment expansions up to
<math id="A2.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{1},\rho^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{1},\rho^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">In Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma B.6 (One-step moment estimates for m-USAM up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1). ‣ B.3 m-USAM ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>, we derived one-step moment estimates for the m-USAM discrete algorithm and, via Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for SDEs). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, for its corresponding SDE update (<a href="#A2.E27" title="In Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>). These estimates demonstrate that the first- and second-order moments satisfy the matching conditions of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem A.2. ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>. Together with the uniform moment bounds from Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ Appendix D Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, we are now ready to establish the main weak-approximation theorem for m-USAM.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.7</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(m-USAM SDE)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Notation and assumption ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote by <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> the m-USAM iterates in (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3.3 SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), and let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{t}\}_{t\in[0,T]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{t}\}_{t\in[0,T]}</annotation></semantics></math> be the solution of the SDE (<a href="#A2.E32" title="In B.3 m-USAM ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>). Suppose:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The functions</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f^{\mathrm{m\text{-}USAM}}\;=\;\nabla\Bigl(f+\frac{\rho}{2}\|\nabla f\|^{2}+\frac{\rho}{2m}\mathrm{tr}(V)\Bigr)\quad\text{and}\quad\sqrt{\Sigma^{\mathrm{m\text{-}USAM}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>USAM</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>USAM</mi></mrow></msup></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f^{\mathrm{m\text{-}USAM}}\;=\;\nabla\Bigl(f+\frac{\rho}{2}\|\nabla f\|^{2}+\frac{\rho}{2m}\mathrm{tr}(V)\Bigr)\quad\text{and}\quad\sqrt{\Sigma^{\mathrm{m\text{-}USAM}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I5.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I5.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">are Lipschitz on </span><math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I5.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The mapping</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{\gamma}(x)\;=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma,|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x+\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\gamma}(x)\;=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma,|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x+\rho\,\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I5.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I5.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfies, almost surely, the Lipschitz condition</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla h_{\gamma}(x)-\nabla h_{\gamma}(y)\|\;\leq\;L_{\gamma}\,\|x-y\|,\qquad\forall\,x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla h_{\gamma}(x)-\nabla h_{\gamma}(y)\|\;\leq\;L_{\gamma}\,\|x-y\|,\qquad\forall\,x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I5.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I5.i2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="A2.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\gamma}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\gamma}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I5.i2.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> a.s. and </span><math id="A2.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[L_{\gamma}^{m}]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[L_{\gamma}^{m}]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I5.i2.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for every </span><math id="A2.I5.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I5.i2.p1.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{t}:t\in[0,T]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{t}:t\in[0,T]\}</annotation></semantics></math> is an order-<math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math> weak approximation of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, namely: for each <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a constant <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta,\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta,\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\Bigl|\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(x_{k})\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(X_{k\eta})\bigr]\Bigr|\;\leq\;C\,\bigl(\eta+\rho^{2}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\Bigl|\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(x_{k})\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(X_{k\eta})\bigr]\Bigr|\;\leq\;C\,\bigl(\eta+\rho^{2}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we verify that SDE (<a href="#A2.E32" title="In B.3 m-USAM ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) admits a unique strong solution.
By assumption, both the drift and diffusion coefficients are globally Lipschitz, which in turn implies a linear-growth condition.
Therefore, Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1 (Existence and Uniqueness of Strong Solutions ( , )). ‣ Appendix D Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> applies and yields the existence and uniqueness of a strong solution on <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, by Lemmas <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for SDEs). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma B.6 (One-step moment estimates for m-USAM up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1). ‣ B.3 m-USAM ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>, and <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ Appendix D Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, all the conditions of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem A.2. ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> are satisfied, and the proof is complete.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark B.8</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Lipschitz conditions are to ensure that the SDE has a unique strong solution with uniformly bounded moments. It is possible to appropriately relax them if we allow weak solutions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mil’shtein,, 1986</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>SDE approximation for SAM variants</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that the update rules of SAM variants are defined by:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{mini-batch SAM:}\quad x_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>mini-batch SAM:</mtext><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{mini-batch SAM:}\quad x_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E34.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{k}-\eta\,\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}(x_{k})}{\|\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}(x_{k})\|}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{k}-\eta\,\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}(x_{k})}{\|\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}(x_{k})\|}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{n-SAM:}\quad x_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>n-SAM:</mtext><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{n-SAM:}\quad x_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E35.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{k}-\eta\,\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f(x_{k})}{\|\nabla f(x_{k})\|}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{k}-\eta\,\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f(x_{k})}{\|\nabla f(x_{k})\|}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{m-SAM:}\quad x_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>m-SAM:</mtext><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{m-SAM:}\quad x_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{k}-\frac{\eta\,m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\|}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{k}-\frac{\eta\,m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\|}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Mini-batch SAM</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the mini-batch SAM algorithm (<a href="#A3.E34" title="In Appendix C SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>), we define the continuous-time approximation <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as the solution to the following SDE:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle dX_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle dX_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\nabla f^{SAM}(X_{t})\,dt+\sqrt{\eta\,\Sigma^{SAM}(X_{t})}\,dW_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\nabla f^{SAM}(X_{t})\,dt+\sqrt{\eta\,\Sigma^{SAM}(X_{t})}\,dW_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A3.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{SAM}(X_{t}):=f(X_{t})+\rho\|\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{SAM}(X_{t}):=f(X_{t})+\rho\|\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{SAM}(X_{t}):=\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t})+\rho\bigl(\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})+\Sigma_{0,1}^{\top}(X_{t})\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{SAM}(X_{t}):=\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t})+\rho\bigl(\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})+\Sigma_{0,1}^{\top}(X_{t})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\left[\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)^{\top}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\left[\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t}))\cdot\bigl(\frac{\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(X_{t})\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})}{\|f_{\gamma}(X_{t})\|}-\mathbb{E}[\frac{\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(X_{t})\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})}{\|f_{\gamma}(X_{t})\|}]\bigr)^{\top}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t}))\cdot\bigl(\frac{\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(X_{t})\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})}{\|f_{\gamma}(X_{t})\|}-\mathbb{E}[\frac{\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(X_{t})\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})}{\|f_{\gamma}(X_{t})\|}]\bigr)^{\top}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(mini-batch SAM SDE, adapted from Theorem 3.5 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Compagnoni et al., (2023)</a></cite>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Notation and assumption ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote by <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> the mini-batch SAM iterates in (<a href="#S1.E4" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), and let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{t}\}_{t\in[0,T]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{t}\}_{t\in[0,T]}</annotation></semantics></math> be the solution of the SDE (<a href="#A3.E37" title="In C.1 Mini-batch SAM ‣ Appendix C SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>). Suppose:</span></p>
<ol id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The functions</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f^{\mathrm{SAM}}\;=\;\nabla\Bigl(f+\rho\|\nabla f\|\Bigr)\quad\text{and}\quad\sqrt{\Sigma^{\mathrm{SAM}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>SAM</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>SAM</mi></msup></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f^{\mathrm{SAM}}\;=\;\nabla\Bigl(f+\rho\|\nabla f\|\Bigr)\quad\text{and}\quad\sqrt{\Sigma^{\mathrm{SAM}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">are Lipschitz on </span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The mapping</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\gamma}(x)\;=\;-\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)\|}\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\gamma}(x)\;=\;-\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)\|}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfies, almost surely, the Lipschitz condition</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla h_{\gamma}(x)-\nabla h_{\gamma}(y)\|\;\leq\;L_{\gamma}\,\|x-y\|,\qquad\forall\,x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla h_{\gamma}(x)-\nabla h_{\gamma}(y)\|\;\leq\;L_{\gamma}\,\|x-y\|,\qquad\forall\,x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\gamma}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\gamma}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> a.s. and </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[L_{\gamma}^{m}]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[L_{\gamma}^{m}]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for every </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{t}:t\in[0,T]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{t}:t\in[0,T]\}</annotation></semantics></math> is an order-<math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math> weak approximation of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, namely: for each <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a constant <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\Bigl|\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(x_{k})\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(X_{k\eta})\bigr]\Bigr|\;\leq\;C\,\bigl(\eta+\rho^{2}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\Bigl|\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(x_{k})\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(X_{k\eta})\bigr]\Bigr|\;\leq\;C\,\bigl(\eta+\rho^{2}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof Sketch.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (mini-batch SAM SDE, adapted from Theorem 3.5 of ( ) ). ‣ C.1 Mini-batch SAM ‣ Appendix C SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> follows by replacing the single-parameter Lemmas A.1, A.2 and A.14 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Compagnoni et al., (2023)</a></cite> with our two-parameter versions—Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem A.2. ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for SDEs). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for the discrete algorithm). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>—imposing the extra global Lipschitz conditions to guarantee existence and uniqueness of the strong solution. We therefore omit the routine algebraic details.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>n-SAM</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the n-SAM algorithm, we define the continuous-time approximation <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as the solution to the following SDE:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle dX_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle dX_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\nabla f^{n\text{-}SAM}(X_{t})\,dt+\sqrt{\eta\,\Sigma^{n\text{-}SAM}(X_{t})}\,dW_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\nabla f^{n\text{-}SAM}(X_{t})\,dt+\sqrt{\eta\,\Sigma^{n\text{-}SAM}(X_{t})}\,dW_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A3.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{n\text{-}SAM}(X_{t}):=f(X_{t})+\rho\|\nabla f(X_{t})\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{n\text{-}SAM}(X_{t}):=f(X_{t})+\rho\|\nabla f(X_{t})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{n\text{-}SAM}(X_{t}):=\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t})+\rho\bigl(\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})+\Sigma_{0,1}^{\top}(X_{t})\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{n\text{-}SAM}(X_{t}):=\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t})+\rho\bigl(\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})+\Sigma_{0,1}^{\top}(X_{t})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\left[\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)^{\top}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\left[\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)\bigl(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t}))\cdot\bigl((\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla^{2}f(X_{t}))\frac{\nabla f(X_{t})}{\|\nabla f(X_{t})\|}\bigr)^{\top}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(\nabla f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t}))\cdot\bigl((\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(X_{t})-\nabla^{2}f(X_{t}))\frac{\nabla f(X_{t})}{\|\nabla f(X_{t})\|}\bigr)^{\top}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by deriving, via the following lemma, a one-step error estimate for the n-SAM discrete algorithm, which will be used to prove the main approximation theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(One-step moment estimates for n-SAM up to <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{1},\rho^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{1},\rho^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Notation and assumption ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{i}f^{\mathrm{n\text{-}SAM}}(x):=\partial_{i}f(x)\;+\;\rho\sum_{j=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{ij}f(x)\,\frac{\partial_{j}f(x)}{\|\nabla f(x)\|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>SAM</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{i}f^{\mathrm{n\text{-}SAM}}(x):=\partial_{i}f(x)\;+\;\rho\sum_{j=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{ij}f(x)\,\frac{\partial_{j}f(x)}{\|\nabla f(x)\|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the one-step increment defined in (<a href="#A1.E24" title="In Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>). Then:</span></p>
<ol id="A3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\bigr]=-\,\partial_{i}f^{\mathrm{n\text{-}SAM}}(x)\,\eta+O(\eta\,\rho^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>SAM</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\bigr]=-\,\partial_{i}f^{\mathrm{n\text{-}SAM}}(x)\,\eta+O(\eta\,\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\,\Delta_{(j)}(x)\bigr]=\eta^{2}\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\,\partial_{j}f(x)+\Sigma^{\mathrm{n\text{-}SAM}}_{(ij)}(x)\Bigr)\;+\;\eta^{2}\,\rho\,\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{jl}f(x)\,\frac{\partial_{l}f(x)}{\|\nabla f(x)\|}+\partial_{j}f(x)\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{il}f(x)\,\frac{\partial_{l}f(x)}{\|\nabla f(x)\|}\Bigr)+O(\eta^{2}\,\rho^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>SAM</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\,\Delta_{(j)}(x)\bigr]=\eta^{2}\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\,\partial_{j}f(x)+\Sigma^{\mathrm{n\text{-}SAM}}_{(ij)}(x)\Bigr)\;+\;\eta^{2}\,\rho\,\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{jl}f(x)\,\frac{\partial_{l}f(x)}{\|\nabla f(x)\|}+\partial_{j}f(x)\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{il}f(x)\,\frac{\partial_{l}f(x)}{\|\nabla f(x)\|}\Bigr)+O(\eta^{2}\,\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl|\Delta_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\Bigr]=O(\eta^{3})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl|\Delta_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\Bigr]=O(\eta^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The n-SAM update is</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{k+1}=x_{k}\;-\;\eta\,\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}\Bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\tfrac{\nabla f(x_{k})}{\|\nabla f(x_{k})\|}\Bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k+1}=x_{k}\;-\;\eta\,\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}\Bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\tfrac{\nabla f(x_{k})}{\|\nabla f(x_{k})\|}\Bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">so</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(x)=x_{k+1}-x_{k}=\eta\,h\bigl(x,\gamma,\rho\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(x)=x_{k+1}-x_{k}=\eta\,h\bigl(x,\gamma,\rho\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">with</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(x,\gamma,\rho):=-\,\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,u(x)\bigr),\qquad u(x):=\frac{\nabla f(x)}{\|\nabla f(x)\|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x,\gamma,\rho):=-\,\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,u(x)\bigr),\qquad u(x):=\frac{\nabla f(x)}{\|\nabla f(x)\|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">By Taylor’s theorem with integral remainder <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Folland,, 2005</a>)</cite>, for each <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and writing <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(x)=\nabla f(x)/\|\nabla f(x)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(x)=\nabla f(x)/\|\nabla f(x)\|</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,u(x)\bigr)=\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)+\rho\,\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(x)\,u(x)+R(x,\gamma,\rho)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,u(x)\bigr)=\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)+\rho\,\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(x)\,u(x)+R(x,\gamma,\rho),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(x,\gamma,\rho)=\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\;D^{3}f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+t\,\rho\,u(x)\bigr)\bigl[\rho\,u(x),\,\rho\,u(x)\bigr]\,dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(x,\gamma,\rho)=\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\;D^{3}f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+t\,\rho\,u(x)\bigr)\bigl[\rho\,u(x),\,\rho\,u(x)\bigr]\,dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{3}f_{\gamma}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{3}f_{\gamma}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the third-order tensor of partial derivatives of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{3}f_{\gamma}(y)[v,w]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{3}f_{\gamma}(y)[v,w]</annotation></semantics></math> its bilinear action on vectors <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v,w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v,w</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma}\in G^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma}\in G^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a polynomially bounded function <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(x)\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(x)\in G</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\|D^{3}f_{\gamma}(y)\bigr\|\;\leq\;K(x),\quad\forall\,y\;\text{with}\;\|y-x\|\leq\rho\,\|u(x)\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>with</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\|D^{3}f_{\gamma}(y)\bigr\|\;\leq\;K(x),\quad\forall\,y\;\text{with}\;\|y-x\|\leq\rho\,\|u(x)\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|R(x,\gamma,\rho)\|\leq\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\,K(x)\,\|\rho\,u(x)\|^{2}\,dt=O(\rho^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|R(x,\gamma,\rho)\|\leq\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\,K(x)\,\|\rho\,u(x)\|^{2}\,dt=O(\rho^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">uniformly in <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(x,\gamma,\rho)=h_{0}(x,\gamma)+\rho\,h_{1}(x,\gamma)+O(\rho^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x,\gamma,\rho)=h_{0}(x,\gamma)+\rho\,h_{1}(x,\gamma)+O(\rho^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">with</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0}(x,\gamma):=-\nabla f_{\gamma}(x),\qquad h_{1}(x,\gamma):=-\,\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(x)\,\frac{\nabla f(x)}{\|\nabla f(x)\|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}(x,\gamma):=-\nabla f_{\gamma}(x),\qquad h_{1}(x,\gamma):=-\,\nabla^{2}f_{\gamma}(x)\,\frac{\nabla f(x)}{\|\nabla f(x)\|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Notation and assumption ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, each <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0},h_{1}\in G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0},h_{1}\in G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[h_{0}(x,\gamma)]=-\nabla f(x),\qquad\mathbb{E}[h_{1}(x,\gamma)]=-\,\nabla^{2}f(x)\,\frac{\nabla f(x)}{\|\nabla f(x)\|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[h_{0}(x,\gamma)]=-\nabla f(x),\qquad\mathbb{E}[h_{1}(x,\gamma)]=-\,\nabla^{2}f(x)\,\frac{\nabla f(x)}{\|\nabla f(x)\|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">The same application of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for the discrete algorithm). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a> then yields the moment expansions (i)–(iii) up to order <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{1},\rho^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{1},\rho^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> as stated.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2 (One-step moment estimates for n-SAM up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1). ‣ C.2 n-SAM ‣ Appendix C SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>, we derived one-step moment estimates for the n-SAM discrete algorithm and, via Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for SDEs). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, for its corresponding SDE update (<a href="#A3.E35" title="In Appendix C SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>). These estimates demonstrate that the first- and second-order moments satisfy the matching conditions of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem A.2. ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>. Together with the uniform moment bounds from Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ Appendix D Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, we are now ready to establish the main weak-approximation theorem for n-SAM.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(n-SAM SDE)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Notation and assumption ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote by <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> the n-SAM iterates in (<a href="#S1.E3" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), and let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{t}\}_{t\in[0,T]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{t}\}_{t\in[0,T]}</annotation></semantics></math> be the solution of the SDE (<a href="#A3.E39" title="In C.2 n-SAM ‣ Appendix C SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>). Suppose:</span></p>
<ol id="A3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The functions</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f^{\mathrm{n\text{-}SAM}}\;=\;\nabla\Bigl(f+\rho\|\nabla f\|\Bigr)\quad\text{and}\quad\sqrt{\Sigma^{\mathrm{n\text{-}SAM}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>SAM</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>SAM</mi></mrow></msup></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f^{\mathrm{n\text{-}SAM}}\;=\;\nabla\Bigl(f+\rho\|\nabla f\|\Bigr)\quad\text{and}\quad\sqrt{\Sigma^{\mathrm{n\text{-}SAM}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">are Lipschitz on </span><math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The mapping</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\gamma}(x)\;=\;-\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f(x)}{\|\nabla f(x)\|}\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\gamma}(x)\;=\;-\nabla f_{\gamma}\bigl(x+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f(x)}{\|\nabla f(x)\|}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfies, almost surely, the Lipschitz condition</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla h_{\gamma}(x)-\nabla h_{\gamma}(y)\|\;\leq\;L_{\gamma}\,\|x-y\|,\qquad\forall\,x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla h_{\gamma}(x)-\nabla h_{\gamma}(y)\|\;\leq\;L_{\gamma}\,\|x-y\|,\qquad\forall\,x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\gamma}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\gamma}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> a.s. and </span><math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[L_{\gamma}^{m}]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[L_{\gamma}^{m}]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for every </span><math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{t}:t\in[0,T]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{t}:t\in[0,T]\}</annotation></semantics></math> is an order-<math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math> weak approximation of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, namely: for each <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a constant <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\Bigl|\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(x_{k})\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(X_{k\eta})\bigr]\Bigr|\;\leq\;C\,\bigl(\eta+\rho^{2}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\Bigl|\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(x_{k})\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(X_{k\eta})\bigr]\Bigr|\;\leq\;C\,\bigl(\eta+\rho^{2}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we verify that SDE (<a href="#A3.E39" title="In C.2 n-SAM ‣ Appendix C SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>) admits a unique strong solution.
By assumption, both the drift and diffusion coefficients are globally Lipschitz, which in turn implies a linear-growth condition.
Therefore, Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1 (Existence and Uniqueness of Strong Solutions ( , )). ‣ Appendix D Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> applies and yields the existence and uniqueness of a strong solution on <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, by Lemmas <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for SDEs). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2 (One-step moment estimates for n-SAM up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1). ‣ C.2 n-SAM ‣ Appendix C SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>, and <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ Appendix D Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, all the conditions of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem A.2. ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> are satisfied, and the proof is complete.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark C.4</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Lipschitz conditions are to ensure that the SDE has a unique strong solution with uniformly bounded moments. It is possible to appropriately relax them if we allow weak solutions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mil’shtein,, 1986</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>m-SAM</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the m-SAM algorithm, we define the continuous-time approximation <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as the solution to the following SDE:</p>
<table id="A3.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="dX_{t}=-\nabla\bigl(f(X_{t})+\frac{\rho}{m}\mathbb{E}\|\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i\in\mathcal{I},\\
|\mathcal{I}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{i}(X_{t})\|\bigr)dt\quad+\sqrt{\frac{m\eta}{|\gamma|}}\left(\Sigma^{m-SAM}(X_{t})\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}dW_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dX_{t}=-\nabla\bigl(f(X_{t})+\frac{\rho}{m}\mathbb{E}\|\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i\in\mathcal{I},\\
|\mathcal{I}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{i}(X_{t})\|\bigr)dt\quad+\sqrt{\frac{m\eta}{|\gamma|}}\left(\Sigma^{m-SAM}(X_{t})\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}dW_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A3.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{m-SAM}(X_{t}):=\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t})+\rho(\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})+\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})^{\top})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{m-SAM}(X_{t}):=\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t})+\rho(\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})+\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t})^{\top}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\left[\bigl(\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)\bigl(\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)^{\top}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{0,0}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\left[\bigl(\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)\bigl(\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t})\bigr)^{\top}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t}))\cdot\bigl(\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})\|}-\mathbb{E}[\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})\|}]\bigr)^{\top}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{0,1}(X_{t}):=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})-\nabla f(X_{t}))\cdot\bigl(\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})\|}-\mathbb{E}[\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(X_{t})\|}]\bigr)^{\top}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by deriving, via the following lemma, a one-step error estimate for the m-sam discrete algorithm, which will be used to prove the main approximation theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.5</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(One-step moment estimates for m-SAM up to <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{1},\rho^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{1},\rho^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Notation and assumption ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{i}f^{m\text{-}SAM}(x)\;:=\;\partial_{i}f(x)\;+\;\rho\,\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\sum_{j=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{ij}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\,\frac{\partial_{j}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\|}\Bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{i}f^{m\text{-}SAM}(x)\;:=\;\partial_{i}f(x)\;+\;\rho\,\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\sum_{j=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{ij}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\,\frac{\partial_{j}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\|}\Bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the one-step increment defined in (<a href="#A1.E24" title="In Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>). Then:</span></p>
<ol id="A3.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\bigr]=-\,\partial_{i}f^{m\text{-}SAM}(x)\,\eta+O(\eta\,\rho^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\bigr]=-\,\partial_{i}f^{m\text{-}SAM}(x)\,\eta+O(\eta\,\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\,\Delta_{(j)}(x)\bigr]=\eta^{2}\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\,\partial_{j}f(x)+\Sigma^{m\text{-}SAM}_{(ij)}(x)\Bigr)\;+\;\eta^{2}\,\rho\,\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\;\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{jl}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\,\frac{\partial_{l}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\|}\Bigr]+\partial_{j}f(x)\;\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{il}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\,\frac{\partial_{l}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\|}\Bigr]\Bigr)+O(\eta^{2}\,\rho^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[\Delta_{(i)}(x)\,\Delta_{(j)}(x)\bigr]=\eta^{2}\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\,\partial_{j}f(x)+\Sigma^{m\text{-}SAM}_{(ij)}(x)\Bigr)\;+\;\eta^{2}\,\rho\,\Bigl(\partial_{i}f(x)\;\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{jl}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\,\frac{\partial_{l}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\|}\Bigr]+\partial_{j}f(x)\;\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\sum_{l=1}^{d}\partial^{2}_{il}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\,\frac{\partial_{l}f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}}(x)\|}\Bigr]\Bigr)+O(\eta^{2}\,\rho^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A3.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl|\Delta_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\Bigr]=O(\eta^{3})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\prod_{j=1}^{3}\bigl|\Delta_{(i_{j})}(x)\bigr|\Bigr]=O(\eta^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that the m-SAM update is</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\frac{\eta\,m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\,|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\Bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\|}\Bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\frac{\eta\,m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\,|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\Bigl(x_{k}+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x_{k})\|}\Bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">so the one-step increment</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(x)=x_{k+1}-x_{k}=\eta\,h(x,\gamma,\rho)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(x)=x_{k+1}-x_{k}=\eta\,h(x,\gamma,\rho),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h(x,\gamma,\rho):=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\,|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\Bigl(x+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x,\gamma,\rho):=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\,|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\Bigl(x+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">By Taylor’s theorem with integral remainder <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Folland,, 2005</a>)</cite>, for each subset index <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\Bigl(x+\rho\,\tfrac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\Bigr)=\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)+\rho\,\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\,\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}+R(x,\gamma,\rho)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\Bigl(x+\rho\,\tfrac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\Bigr)=\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)+\rho\,\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\,\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}+R(x,\gamma,\rho),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(x,\gamma,\rho)=\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\;D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\Bigl(x+t\,\rho\,\tfrac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\Bigr)\bigl[\rho\,\tfrac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|},\,\rho\,\tfrac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\bigr]\,dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(x,\gamma,\rho)=\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\;D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\Bigl(x+t\,\rho\,\tfrac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\Bigr)\bigl[\rho\,\tfrac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|},\,\rho\,\tfrac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\bigr]\,dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> is the third-order derivative tensor of <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(y)[u,v]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(y)[u,v]</annotation></semantics></math> its action on <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\in G^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\in G^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(x)\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(x)\in G</annotation></semantics></math> polynomially bounded so that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(y)\|\leq K(x)\quad\text{whenever}\quad\|y-x\|\leq\rho\,\Bigl\|\tfrac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\Bigr\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>whenever</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|D^{3}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(y)\|\leq K(x)\quad\text{whenever}\quad\|y-x\|\leq\rho\,\Bigl\|\tfrac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\Bigr\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|R(x,\gamma,\rho)\|\leq\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\,K(x)\,\|\rho\,\tfrac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\|^{2}\,dt=\tfrac{1}{2}K(x)\,\rho^{2}=O(\rho^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|R(x,\gamma,\rho)\|\leq\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)\,K(x)\,\|\rho\,\tfrac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\|^{2}\,dt=\tfrac{1}{2}K(x)\,\rho^{2}=O(\rho^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">uniformly in <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus a Taylor expansion in <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(x,\gamma,\rho)=h_{0}(x,\gamma)+\rho\,h_{1}(x,\gamma)+O(\rho^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x,\gamma,\rho)=h_{0}(x,\gamma)+\rho\,h_{1}(x,\gamma)+O(\rho^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">with</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{0}(x,\gamma):=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\,|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x),\quad h_{1}(x,\gamma):=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\,|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\,\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}(x,\gamma):=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\,|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x),\quad h_{1}(x,\gamma):=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma_{k},\,|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\,\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Notation and assumption ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, each <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0},h_{1}\in G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0},h_{1}\in G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[h_{0}(x,\gamma)]=-\nabla f(x),\quad\mathbb{E}[h_{1}(x,\gamma)]=-\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\,\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\Bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[h_{0}(x,\gamma)]=-\nabla f(x),\quad\mathbb{E}[h_{1}(x,\gamma)]=-\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\nabla^{2}f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\,\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\Bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">Applying Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for the discrete algorithm). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a> to these <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0},h_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0},h_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> yields exactly the three moment estimates up to <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{1},\rho^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{1},\rho^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> as claimed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma C.5 (One-step moment estimates for m-SAM up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1). ‣ C.3 m-SAM ‣ Appendix C SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>, we derived one-step moment estimates for the m-SAM discrete algorithm and, via Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for SDEs). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, for its corresponding SDE update (<a href="#A3.E36" title="In Appendix C SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>). These estimates demonstrate that the first- and second-order moments satisfy the matching conditions of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem A.2. ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>. Together with the uniform moment bounds from Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ Appendix D Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, we are now ready to establish the main weak-approximation theorem for m-SAM.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.6</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(m-SAM SDE)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Notation and assumption ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ Appendix B SDE approximation for USAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote by <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> the m-SAM iterates in (<a href="#S1.E5" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), and let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{t}\}_{t\in[0,T]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{t}\}_{t\in[0,T]}</annotation></semantics></math> be the solution of the SDE (<a href="#A3.E41" title="In C.3 m-SAM ‣ Appendix C SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>). Suppose:</span></p>
<ol id="A3.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A3.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The functions</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f^{\mathrm{m\text{-}SAM}}\;=-\nabla\bigl(f+\frac{\rho}{m}\mathbb{E}\|\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i\in\mathcal{I},\\
|\mathcal{I}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{i}\|\bigr)\quad\text{and}\quad\sqrt{\Sigma^{\mathrm{m\text{-}SAM}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>SAM</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>SAM</mi></mrow></msup></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f^{\mathrm{m\text{-}SAM}}\;=-\nabla\bigl(f+\frac{\rho}{m}\mathbb{E}\|\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i\in\mathcal{I},\\
|\mathcal{I}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{i}\|\bigr)\quad\text{and}\quad\sqrt{\Sigma^{\mathrm{m\text{-}SAM}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I5.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I5.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">are Lipschitz on </span><math id="A3.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I5.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A3.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The mapping</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex119" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{\gamma}(x)\;=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma,|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\gamma}(x)\;=-\frac{m}{|\gamma|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{I}_{j}\subset\gamma,|\mathcal{I}_{j}|=m\end{subarray}}\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}\bigl(x+\rho\,\frac{\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)}{\|\nabla f_{\mathcal{I}_{j}}(x)\|}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I5.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I5.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfies, almost surely, the Lipschitz condition</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex120" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla h_{\gamma}(x)-\nabla h_{\gamma}(y)\|\;\leq\;L_{\gamma}\,\|x-y\|,\qquad\forall\,x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla h_{\gamma}(x)-\nabla h_{\gamma}(y)\|\;\leq\;L_{\gamma}\,\|x-y\|,\qquad\forall\,x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I5.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I5.i2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="A3.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\gamma}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\gamma}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I5.i2.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> a.s. and </span><math id="A3.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[L_{\gamma}^{m}]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[L_{\gamma}^{m}]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I5.i2.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for every </span><math id="A3.I5.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I5.i2.p1.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{t}:t\in[0,T]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{t}:t\in[0,T]\}</annotation></semantics></math> is an order-<math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math> weak approximation of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, namely: for each <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a constant <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\Bigl|\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(x_{k})\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(X_{k\eta})\bigr]\Bigr|\;\leq\;C\,\bigl(\eta+\rho^{2}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\Bigl|\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(x_{k})\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[g(X_{k\eta})\bigr]\Bigr|\;\leq\;C\,\bigl(\eta+\rho^{2}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we verify that SDE (<a href="#A3.E41" title="In C.3 m-SAM ‣ Appendix C SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) admits a unique strong solution.
By assumption, both the drift and diffusion coefficients are globally Lipschitz, which in turn implies a linear-growth condition.
Therefore, Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1 (Existence and Uniqueness of Strong Solutions ( , )). ‣ Appendix D Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> applies and yields the existence and uniqueness of a strong solution on <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, by Lemmas <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (One-step moment estimates up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1 for SDEs). ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma C.5 (One-step moment estimates for m-SAM up to 𝜂^1,𝜌^1). ‣ C.3 m-SAM ‣ Appendix C SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>, and <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ Appendix D Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, all the conditions of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem A.2. ‣ Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> are satisfied, and the proof is complete.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark C.7</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Lipschitz conditions are to ensure that the SDE has a unique strong solution with uniformly bounded moments. It is possible to appropriately relax them if we allow weak solutions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mil’shtein,, 1986</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Auxiliary Lemmas</h2>

<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Existence and Uniqueness of Strong Solutions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Evans,, 2012</a>)</cite>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}</annotation></semantics></math> be measurable functions satisfying:</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Global Lipschitz.</span><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> There exists a constant </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex122" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|b(x)-b(y)\|\;+\;\|\sigma(x)-\sigma(y)\|\;\leq\;L\,\|x-y\|,\quad\forall\,x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|b(x)-b(y)\|\;+\;\|\sigma(x)-\sigma(y)\|\;\leq\;L\,\|x-y\|,\quad\forall\,x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Linear growth.</span><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> There exists a constant </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex123" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|b(x)\|^{2}\;+\;\|\sigma(x)\|^{2}\;\leq\;K\,\bigl(1+\|x\|^{2}\bigr),\quad\forall\,x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|b(x)\|^{2}\;+\;\|\sigma(x)\|^{2}\;\leq\;K\,\bigl(1+\|x\|^{2}\bigr),\quad\forall\,x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>-valued random variable with <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\|X_{0}\|^{2}]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\|X_{0}\|^{2}]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the SDE</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex124" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dX_{t}=b(X_{t})\,dt+\sigma(X_{t})\,dW_{t},\quad X_{0}\text{ given}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> given</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dX_{t}=b(X_{t})\,dt+\sigma(X_{t})\,dW_{t},\quad X_{0}\text{ given},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">admits a unique strong solution <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{t}\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{t}\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex125" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\sup_{0\leq s\leq T}\|X_{s}\|^{2}\Bigr]&lt;\infty,\quad\forall\,T&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\sup_{0\leq s\leq T}\|X_{s}\|^{2}\Bigr]&lt;\infty,\quad\forall\,T&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(</span><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al.,, 2019</a><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">)</span></cite><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{k}:k\geq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{k}:k\geq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the generalized iterations defined in (<a href="#A1.E22" title="In Appendix A General theory for two-parameter weak approximation. ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>). Suppose</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex126" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|h(x,\gamma,\eta)\bigr|\;\leq\;L_{\gamma}\bigl(1+\|x\|\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|h(x,\gamma,\eta)\bigr|\;\leq\;L_{\gamma}\bigl(1+\|x\|\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\gamma}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\gamma}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely and</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex127" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[L_{\gamma}^{m}\bigr]&lt;\infty\quad\text{for all }m\geq 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[L_{\gamma}^{m}\bigr]&lt;\infty\quad\text{for all }m\geq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then for any fixed <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the moment <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|x_{k}\|^{m}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|x_{k}\|^{m}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math> exists and is uniformly bounded in both <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,1,\dots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,1,\dots,N</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\lfloor T/\eta\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem9" title="Proposition 3.9. ‣ 3.4 SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a></h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We will use the following lemma on convex order to prove Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem9" title="Proposition 3.9. ‣ 3.4 SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a>, whose proof can be found in classical textbooks on stochastic order, such as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Müller and Stoyan, (2002)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Convex-order Monotonicity)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\dots,X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\dots,X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be i.i.d. random vectors in <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with a log-concave density. For each integer <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq k\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq k\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{k}\;=\;\frac{1}{k}\sum_{i=1}^{k}X_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{k}\;=\;\frac{1}{k}\sum_{i=1}^{k}X_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then for any <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq k&lt;m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq k&lt;m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math> and any convex function <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\phi(S_{m})\bigr]\;\leq\;\mathbb{E}\bigl[\phi(S_{k})\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\phi(S_{m})\bigr]\;\leq\;\mathbb{E}\bigl[\phi(S_{k})\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem9" title="Proposition 3.9. ‣ 3.4 SDE approximation for SAM variants ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Lower bound:
Applying Jensen’s inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex130" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla f(x)\|=\bigl\|\mathbb{E}[\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)]\bigr\|\leq\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)\|]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla f(x)\|=\bigl\|\mathbb{E}[\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)]\bigr\|\leq\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)\|].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Upper bound: By Cauchy–Schwarz inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex131" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)\|]\leq\sqrt{\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)\|^{2}]}=\sqrt{\|\nabla f(x)\|^{2}+\frac{\mathrm{tr}(V(x))}{|\gamma|}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)\|]\leq\sqrt{\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla f_{\gamma}(x)\|^{2}]}=\sqrt{\|\nabla f(x)\|^{2}+\frac{\mathrm{tr}(V(x))}{|\gamma|}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Combining both bounds completes the proof of the first statement.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the second statement, we apply Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma E.1 (Convex-order Monotonicity). ‣ Appendix E Proof of Proposition ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a> to the convex function <math id="A5.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math>, which concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Additional Related Works</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theoretical understanding of SAM.</span>
Although SAM and its variants have achieved remarkable success in various practical applications <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Foret et al.,, 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon et al.,, 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kaddour et al.,, 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024b, </a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li and Giannakis,, 2024</a>)</cite>, the theoretical understanding behind them remains limited. The pioneering work of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Andriushchenko and Flammarion, (2022)</a></cite> provided the first theoretical framework for understanding SAM, covering its convergence properties and implicit bias in simple network structures, while also systematically illustrating several empirical phenomena. Subsequently, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Si and Yun, (2024)</a></cite> extended the convergence analysis to various deterministic and stochastic settings. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Compagnoni et al., (2023)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo et al., (2025)</a></cite> conducted an in-depth analysis of the dynamics of SAM using the SDE framework previously developed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., (2017)</a></cite>, leading to a deeper understanding of its implicit bias. On the other hand, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wen et al., (2022)</a></cite> investigated the implicit bias of SAM by analyzing its slow ordinary differential equation (ODE) behavior near the minimizer manifold, demonstrating how SAM drifts toward flatter minima. More recently, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al., (2024)</a></cite> studied the late-stage behavior of SAM using stability analysis, showing its advantage in escaping sharp minima.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Derivation of the Finite Difference Estimator in Equation (<a href="#S4.E21" title="In 4 Practical Method ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>)</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We start with the first-order Taylor expansion around <math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A7.Ex132" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{f_{i}\bigl(x+\delta\,z\bigr)-f_{i}(x)}{\delta}\;=\;\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z\;+\;O(\delta)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{f_{i}\bigl(x+\delta\,z\bigr)-f_{i}(x)}{\delta}\;=\;\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z\;+\;O(\delta),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\{\pm 1\}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\{\pm 1\}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a Rademacher random vector, and <math id="A7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is assumed twice differentiable so that the remainder is of order <math id="A7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: Square both sides.</h4>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Bigl(\tfrac{f_{i}(x+\delta z)-f_{i}(x)}{\delta}\Bigr)^{2}\;=\;\bigl(\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z\bigr)^{2}\;+\;2\bigl(\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z\bigr)\;O(\delta)\;+\;O(\delta)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>z</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn> 2</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>z</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl(\tfrac{f_{i}(x+\delta z)-f_{i}(x)}{\delta}\Bigr)^{2}\;=\;\bigl(\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z\bigr)^{2}\;+\;2\bigl(\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z\bigr)\;O(\delta)\;+\;O(\delta)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Often we simply write this as</p>
<table id="A7.Ex134" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bigl(\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z+O(\delta)\bigr)^{2}\;=\;\bigl(\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z\bigr)^{2}\;+\;O(\delta)\,\bigl(\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z\bigr)\;+\;O(\delta^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>z</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>z</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z+O(\delta)\bigr)^{2}\;=\;\bigl(\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z\bigr)^{2}\;+\;O(\delta)\,\bigl(\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z\bigr)\;+\;O(\delta^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Take expectation over <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> has independent <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pm 1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pm 1\}</annotation></semantics></math> components, we have</p>
<table id="A7.Ex135" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{z}\Bigl[\bigl(\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z\bigr)^{2}\Bigr]\;=\;\bigl\|\nabla f_{i}(x)\bigr\|^{2}\quad\text{(standard Rademacher property)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>z</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext>(standard Rademacher property)</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{z}\Bigl[\bigl(\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z\bigr)^{2}\Bigr]\;=\;\bigl\|\nabla f_{i}(x)\bigr\|^{2}\quad\text{(standard Rademacher property)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence,</p>
<table id="A7.Ex136" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{z}\!\Bigl[\Bigl(\tfrac{f_{i}(x+\delta z)-f_{i}(x)}{\delta}\Bigr)^{2}\Bigr]\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{z}\bigl[\bigl(\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z\bigr)^{2}\bigr]\;+\;O(\delta)\;=\;\|\nabla f_{i}(x)\|^{2}+O(\delta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>z</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{z}\!\Bigl[\Bigl(\tfrac{f_{i}(x+\delta z)-f_{i}(x)}{\delta}\Bigr)^{2}\Bigr]\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{z}\bigl[\bigl(\nabla f_{i}(x)^{\top}z\bigr)^{2}\bigr]\;+\;O(\delta)\;=\;\|\nabla f_{i}(x)\|^{2}+O(\delta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus the mean-squared estimate of the finite difference quotient differs from <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla f_{i}(x)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla f_{i}(x)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by an <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> bias term.
We compare two <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional random vectors <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A7.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rademacher:</span> each component <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is independently <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 1</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Gaussian:</span> each component <math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is i.i.d. <math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Both have <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[z_{j}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[z_{j}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[z_{j}^{2}]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[z_{j}^{2}]=1</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[(z^{\top}v)^{2}]=\|v\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[(z^{\top}v)^{2}]=\|v\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We look at the <em id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">fourth moment</em> <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[(z^{\top}v)^{4}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[(z^{\top}v)^{4}]</annotation></semantics></math>, relevant to the variance in many finite-difference or gradient estimators.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Rademacher case.</h4>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{j}^{2}\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{j}^{2}\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A7.Ex137" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z^{\top}v)^{2}=\bigl(\sum_{j=1}^{d}v_{j}z_{j}\bigr)^{2}=\sum_{j,k}v_{j}v_{k}\,z_{j}z_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z^{\top}v)^{2}=\bigl(\sum_{j=1}^{d}v_{j}z_{j}\bigr)^{2}=\sum_{j,k}v_{j}v_{k}\,z_{j}z_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then</p>
<table id="A7.Ex138" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z^{\top}v)^{4}=\Bigl(\sum_{j,k}v_{j}v_{k}\,z_{j}z_{k}\Bigr)^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z^{\top}v)^{4}=\Bigl(\sum_{j,k}v_{j}v_{k}\,z_{j}z_{k}\Bigr)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and using <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[z_{j}^{4}]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[z_{j}^{4}]=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[z_{j}^{2}z_{k}^{2}]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[z_{j}^{2}z_{k}^{2}]=1</annotation></semantics></math> (when <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq k</annotation></semantics></math>) with zero cross terms of odd product, one obtains a relatively small constant factor.
Detailed calculation yields</p>
<table id="A7.Ex139" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[(z^{\top}v)^{4}\bigr]=\sum_{j=1}^{d}v_{j}^{4}+6\sum_{j&lt;k}v_{j}^{2}v_{k}^{2}\leq 3\,\bigl\|v\bigr\|^{4}\quad(\text{for }d&gt;1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[(z^{\top}v)^{4}\bigr]=\sum_{j=1}^{d}v_{j}^{4}+6\sum_{j&lt;k}v_{j}^{2}v_{k}^{2}\leq 3\,\bigl\|v\bigr\|^{4}\quad(\text{for }d&gt;1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Gaussian case.</h4>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[z_{j}^{4}]=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[z_{j}^{4}]=3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[z_{j}^{2}z_{k}^{2}]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[z_{j}^{2}z_{k}^{2}]=1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq k</annotation></semantics></math>. One can show</p>
<table id="A7.Ex140" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[(z^{\top}v)^{4}]=3\|v\|^{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[(z^{\top}v)^{4}]=3\|v\|^{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence the constant factor in front of <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v\|^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v\|^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> is exactly <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> for Gaussian.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conclusion.</h4>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <em id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">both</em> Rademacher and Gaussian vectors, <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[(z^{\top}v)^{2}]=\|v\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[(z^{\top}v)^{2}]=\|v\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<em id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">However</em>, when analyzing higher-order moments (e.g. <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z^{\top}v)^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z^{\top}v)^{4}</annotation></semantics></math>) that affect the variance of many finite-difference or random-direction estimators, the Rademacher distribution can yield a smaller constant factor. This often leads to reduced variance and tighter theoretical bounds for the same sample size.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Derivation of the Gibbs Distribution (<a href="#S4.E20" title="In 4 Practical Method ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>)</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the following maximization problem :</p>
<table id="A8.Ex141" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{P\in\Delta}\quad\sum_{i\in\gamma}p_{i}\,\left\lVert\nabla f_{i}(x)\right\rVert\;+\;\frac{\mathbb{H}(P)}{\lambda}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></munder><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{P\in\Delta}\quad\sum_{i\in\gamma}p_{i}\,\left\lVert\nabla f_{i}(x)\right\rVert\;+\;\frac{\mathbb{H}(P)}{\lambda},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability simplex (i.e., <math id="A8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}p_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}p_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>),
<math id="A8.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{H}(P)=-\sum_{i}p_{i}\ln p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>ln</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}(P)=-\sum_{i}p_{i}\ln p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the entropy term,
and <math id="A8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a given constant.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">1. Construct the Lagrangian.
We introduce the constraint <math id="A8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}p_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}p_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> with a Lagrange multiplier <math id="A8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A8.Ex142" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}(P,\alpha)\;=\;\sum_{i}p_{i}\,\left\lVert\nabla f_{i}(x)\right\rVert\;+\;\frac{1}{\lambda}\bigl(-\sum_{i}p_{i}\ln p_{i}\bigr)\;+\;\alpha\Bigl(1-\sum_{i}p_{i}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>ln</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(P,\alpha)\;=\;\sum_{i}p_{i}\,\left\lVert\nabla f_{i}(x)\right\rVert\;+\;\frac{1}{\lambda}\bigl(-\sum_{i}p_{i}\ln p_{i}\bigr)\;+\;\alpha\Bigl(1-\sum_{i}p_{i}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">2. Differentiate w.r.t. <math id="A8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and set to zero.
Taking partial derivatives with respect to <math id="A8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and setting them to zero,</p>
<table id="A8.Ex143" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial p_{i}}=\left\lVert\nabla f_{i}(x)\right\rVert-\frac{1}{\lambda}(\ln p_{i}+1)-\alpha=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial p_{i}}=\left\lVert\nabla f_{i}(x)\right\rVert-\frac{1}{\lambda}(\ln p_{i}+1)-\alpha=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A8.Ex144" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\nabla f_{i}(x)\right\rVert-\frac{\ln p_{i}+1}{\lambda}-\alpha=0\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;p_{i}=\exp\!\bigl(\lambda\,\left\lVert\nabla f_{i}(x)\right\rVert+1-\lambda\,\alpha\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.838em" rspace="0.838em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\nabla f_{i}(x)\right\rVert-\frac{\ln p_{i}+1}{\lambda}-\alpha=0\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;p_{i}=\exp\!\bigl(\lambda\,\left\lVert\nabla f_{i}(x)\right\rVert+1-\lambda\,\alpha\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p4.1" class="ltx_p">3. Enforce the normalization.
The constraint <math id="A8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}p_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}p_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> fixes the value of <math id="A8.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>; it amounts to one overall normalization factor in the denominator. Hence the solution takes the well-known Gibbs distribution form:</p>
<table id="A8.Ex145" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}^{*}=\frac{\exp\bigl(\lambda\,\left\lVert\nabla f_{i}(x)\right\rVert\bigr)}{\sum_{j}\exp\bigl(\lambda\,\left\lVert\nabla f_{j}(x)\right\rVert\bigr)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}^{*}=\frac{\exp\bigl(\lambda\,\left\lVert\nabla f_{i}(x)\right\rVert\bigr)}{\sum_{j}\exp\bigl(\lambda\,\left\lVert\nabla f_{j}(x)\right\rVert\bigr)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Algorithm: Reweighted-SAM</h2>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Reweighted-SAM</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> not converged <span id="alg1.l1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
            Forward pass to obtain <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma_{k}}(x_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma_{k}}(x_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=1,\dots,Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=1,\dots,Q</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
             Estimate per-sample gradient norm using Eq. (<a href="#S4.E21" title="In 4 Practical Method ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
            Normalize estimated per-sample gradient norm

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute weight <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. (<a href="#S4.E20" title="In 4 Practical Method ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute perturbation <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> using Eq. (<a href="#S4.E18" title="In 4 Practical Method ‣ Unveiling m-Sharpness Through the Structure of Stochastic Gradient Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute perturbed gradient <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{k}=\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}(x_{k}+\rho\epsilon_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{k}=\nabla f_{\gamma_{k}}(x_{k}+\rho\epsilon_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
            
            
            Update model parameters: <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\eta g_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\eta g_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A10" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix J </span>Additional Experiment Results</h2>

<div id="A10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments were run on NVIDIA RTX 4090 GPUs.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A10.T6" class="ltx_table">
